 "report": {
  "answer": "Five seated judges (anthropic/opus, openai/codex-cli-default, google/gemini, xai/grok, mistral/mistral-large) score the tournament. Independence is mechanical: a judge is independent of an artifact iff the recusal detector in conflicts.py returns eligible. Panel size is 5. Vendor-diversity minimum is 3 distinct vendors computed from the seated roster (measured 5); model-diversity minimum is 3 (measured 5). Hard rule: no judge scores an artifact they or their vendor authored; catalog assignment and disk provenance are both authorship signals. Recusal is dispatch-layer, ignores self-declaration, and hides reasons from the judge. Before scoring a judge may see de-identified dossier bytes, the hashed rubric, and opaque labels; they may not see architecture names, provenance, peer scores, or recusal reasons. Quorum is 3 eligible judges per artifact; below that the verdict is VOID. Lens census: 3/63 files present; 60 absent; 61 provenance gaps; 2 catalog-vs-disk mismatches. SUCCESS:ARC-0066",
